Compare the present-day concentrations of the four gases offered:
carbon dioxide, about 420 parts per million;
methane, about 1.9 parts per million;
nitrous oxide, about 0.33 parts per million;
chlorofluorocarbons, a few parts per billion.
Carbon dioxide exceeds the next largest by more than two hundred times, so it is present in the largest concentration.
Matches option C.

Compare typical albedo values:
fresh snow, 0.80 to 0.90;
forest, 0.10 to 0.20;
ocean water, 0.06 to 0.10 for a high Sun;
asphalt road, 0.05 to 0.10.
Fresh snow returns the largest fraction of the incident radiation and so has the highest albedo, which is why snow-covered ground stays cold.
Matches option A.
